:: day0_npc_aldric_gift [nobr]
<<npcPortrait "aldric" "Aldric">>
<h3>The Empty Yard — Aldric's Gift</h3>

<p>The training yard is empty. No recruits, no guards, no Aldric. Just the flagstones and the weapon racks and the morning light and the replacement training dummy standing where the one I destroyed yesterday stood — fresh leather, new straw, untouched. Someone repaired the world overnight while I was staring at ceilings.</p>

<p>On the weapon rack, something that wasn't there before. A practice sword — not the standard issue from the armoury. Smaller. Lighter. The grip wrapped in new leather, sized for a narrower hand. The balance point adjusted forward for a shorter reach. Beside it, a piece of parchment.</p>

<p><em>Your Highness.</em></p>

<p><em>I had the armourer make this overnight. The grip is for a smaller hand. The weight is adjusted for a lighter frame. The balance is set for someone approximately five inches shorter.</em></p>

<p><em>I don't know what's happening today. I know enough.</em></p>

<p><em>When you're ready to train again, this will be waiting.</em></p>

<p><em>— Aldric</em></p>

<p>He doesn't say what he knows. He doesn't need to. He read the signs — the same signs Caedric read, the same signs the senior maids read, the same signs the entire palace has been reading for three days. And his response is not panic, not judgment, not political calculation. His response is to commission a sword.</p>

<p>This man. This impossibly, infuriatingly good man. His prince is about to become someone else and his first thought is <em>she'll need a weapon that fits.</em></p>

<p>I pick up the practice sword. It's too light for my current hands, too small for my current grip. But tomorrow — tomorrow it will be right. Tomorrow these hands will be smaller, and this grip will fit, and Aldric will stand in this yard and teach me to fight all over again in a body I don't know yet.</p>

<p>I set the sword back on the rack. I take the parchment. I fold it and put it in my pocket, next to the crumpled list with every item crossed off and the Veltham letter. Three pieces of paper that describe the architecture of this week: the trap, the intelligence, and the love.</p>

<<set $d0_npc_aldric_gift to true>>
<<set $affAldric += 5>>
<<set $statRES += 3>>
<<set $stress -= 5>>
<<set $hasAldricSword to true>>
<<set $hasAldricLetter to true>>
<<addItem "aldric_letter" "Aldric's Letter" "A note from the armoury: a practice sword sized for the body you'll wake up in.">>

<div class="scene-end">
  [[Continue → |day0_training]]
</div>
